    {
      "id": "odyssey-c1-s1",
      "chapterId": "chapter-1",
      "name": "The Other Shore",
      "atmosphere": {
        "water": 0.13,
        "wind": 0.025,
        "birds": 0.014,
        "village": 0,
        "music": 0.008
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-frame",
          "type": "action",
          "duration": 1000,
          "effects": {
            "view": "shore",
            "chapter": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-clarity-home",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Odysseus was the king of Ithaca. He had left his wife, Penelope, and their son to fight in the war at Troy."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-clarity-time",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "The war was over, but his journey home had gone wrong. We meet him years later, alone on Calypso’s island."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-p1",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "Every morning, Odysseus watched the sea."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-p2",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "After losing his ship and companions at sea, he had washed up here. Calypso sheltered him, but would not let him leave."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-pace-along-the-shore",
          "type": "action",
          "duration": 2200,
          "effects": {
            "actors": {
              "odysseus": {
                "x": 880,
                "y": 950,
                "facing": "right",
                "pose": "walk"
              }
            }
          },
          "paths": {
            "odysseus": [
              {
                "x": 835,
                "y": 953
              },
              {
                "x": 880,
                "y": 950
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-look-out-to-sea",
          "type": "action",
          "duration": 900,
          "effects": {
            "actors": {
              "odysseus": {
                "facing": "back"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-return-to-the-shore",
          "type": "action",
          "duration": 2200,
          "effects": {
            "actors": {
              "odysseus": {
                "x": 790,
                "y": 955,
                "facing": "left",
                "pose": "walk"
              }
            }
          },
          "paths": {
            "odysseus": [
              {
                "x": 835,
                "y": 953
              },
              {
                "x": 790,
                "y": 955
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-face-the-water-again",
          "type": "action",
          "duration": 450,
          "effects": {
            "actors": {
              "odysseus": {
                "facing": "back"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-p3",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "This shore had kept him alive for years. It had begun to feel like the edge of his life."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-p4",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "Ahead of him was the one thing it could not offer: a way to leave."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-p5",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "He had survived a war. He had survived the sea. Now he was surviving another quiet morning."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-p6",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "Far across the sea lay Ithaca. Penelope still lived there with their son, Telemachus, who had grown up while he was away."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-p7",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "He could remember the weight of an oar. The sound of his son’s voice was becoming harder."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-p8",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "He watched the water until the sunlight hurt his eyes."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s1-p9",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "There was no ship on the water. Still, he looked."
        }
      ],
      "estimatedSeconds": 102
    },
    {
      "id": "odyssey-c1-s2",
      "chapterId": "chapter-1",
      "name": "A Life Without an Ending",
      "atmosphere": {
        "water": 0.13,
        "wind": 0.025,
        "birds": 0.014,
        "village": 0,
        "music": 0.008
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s2-frame",
          "type": "action",
          "duration": 1000,
          "effects": {
            "view": "calypso-entry",
            "chapter": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c1-s2-calypso-approaches",
